# OpenPAVE four-dimension recipe: DGX Spark brain -> RPi5 USB camera body over the seam plugin.
#
# Same shape as configs/dgx-puppypi.env, but the body endpoint is a *sensor* (sensing capability)
# instead of an actuator. See docs/openpave-platform-spec.md and docs/validation-matrix.md.
#
#   1. Brain-side node   : DGX Spark                         -> BRAIN_HOST / BRAIN_PYTHON
#   2. Body endpoint     : RPi5 + USB camera (V4L2)          -> ROBOT_ADAPTER=camera_usb / CAMERA_DEVICE
#   3. Seam transport    : raw_zenoh | device_connect        -> SEAM_TRANSPORT   (swap this line)
#   4. Inference / app   : vLLM / OpenAI-compatible VLM       -> INFERENCE_RUNTIME / UI_*
#
# CONTROL / DATA PLANE SPLIT (important): over the seam, `get_image` is a *query* capability whose
# result is small **control-plane metadata** only ({encoding, bytes, width, height, source, seq}).
# The JPEG frame itself travels on a **separate data plane** (a compressed-image channel), which
# `scripts/seam_run.sh` does NOT carry. For the full frame delivery path see `experiments/camera-mve/`
# (`sensor_body_node.py` + `get_image.py`). This recipe exercises the sensing control plane over the
# seam; it does not move image bytes.
#
# STATUS: validated 2026-09-02 (control plane). DGX brain drove the RPi5 USB camera over the seam via
# scripts/seam_run.sh: `get_image` returned real control-plane metadata (jpeg, ~98 KB, 640x480,
# /dev/video0) over BOTH transports (raw_zenoh and device_connect). The image data plane (frame bytes)
# is separate and NOT carried by seam_run.sh — see experiments/camera-mve. The RPi5 body python
# (BODY_PYTHON) needs OpenCV: `pip install opencv-python-headless` (cv2) plus eclipse-zenoh, and
# device-connect-edge for the device_connect transport.
#
# One-command run (once cv2 is installed on the RPi5):
#   body  (on RPi5): scripts/seam_run.sh configs/dgx-rpicam.env body
#   brain (on DGX) : scripts/seam_run.sh configs/dgx-rpicam.env brain send get_image

# --- dimension 1: brain-side node ---
BRAIN_HOST=192.168.0.24
BRAIN_PYTHON=$HOME/.venv-zenoh/bin/python

# --- dimension 2: body endpoint (sensor) ---
BODY_HOST=192.168.0.21
BODY_PYTHON=$HOME/.venv-zenoh/bin/python   # needs cv2 (opencv-python) for the real USB camera
ROBOT_ADAPTER=camera_usb
CAMERA_DEVICE=/dev/video0

# --- dimension 3: seam transport (the swappable plugin dimension) ---
SEAM_TRANSPORT=raw_zenoh
SEAM_ZENOH_PORT=7447

# --- dimension 4: inference / upper-layer application ---
# Today this is the OpenAI-compatible VLM API used by the /pave baseline path; a registered
# create_inference_runtime(name) plugin surface is roadmap (INFERENCE_RUNTIME names the intent).
INFERENCE_RUNTIME=vllm_openai
UI_MODEL=llava-hf/llava-v1.6-mistral-7b-hf
UI_API_BASE=http://192.168.0.24:8000/v1
